        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: புண்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "புண் — puṇ — \"a sore; an ulcer\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "வாயில் புண் இருந்ததால் காரமாகச் சாப்பிட முடியவில்லை. vāyil puṇ iruntatāl kāramākac cāppiṭa muṭiyavillai. I had a mouth ulcer, so I could not eat spicy food."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "வாய்ப் புண் (puṇ), a mouth ulcer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "புண் (puṇ) is native Dravidian (DEDR 4268), for a wound or sore."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
